.\" Kept in step with `samath --help` and the options table in README.md:
.\" test/docs.sh fails when an option is in one of them and not the others.
.TH SAMATH 1 "" "samath 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
samath \- ask arithmetic questions from a SaMathAPI and mark the answers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samath
.RI [ options ]
.I QUESTIONS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B samath
fetches
.I QUESTIONS
arithmetic tasks from a SaMathAPI server and asks them one at a time. Each
answer is a single key, A, B, C or D, with no Enter needed. Q, or Ctrl-D,
stops the run early. At the end it lists the mistakes, each with the right
answer and the one given, and the score and the time taken. Ctrl-C does the
same and then ends the run by SIGINT.
.PP
Options may come before or after the number of questions. Short options can
be joined, as in
.BR \-pf ,
or a value can follow the option letter directly, as in
.BR \-pt30 .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-time\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Give each question that many seconds to answer, from 1 to 3600. A question
that runs out of time counts as a mistake.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-total\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Give the whole run that many seconds of answering, from 1 to 3600. The time
is counted as the time limit is, so time spent waiting for the server does not
count. When it runs out, the question on
the screen counts as a mistake if it was not answered, and the questions not
reached are not asked. Practice does not run after such a run.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-seed\fR \fINUMBER\fR
Ask the same questions every time, from 0 to 4294967295. The seed is passed
to the API, which has to support it.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-practice\fR
When the run is over, ask the mistakes again, round after round, until each
has been put right. Q stops the practice, and a run that was stopped does not
go on to it.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-length\fR \fIN\fR
Ask for questions of
.I N
numbers each, from 2 to 12.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-brackets\fR
Ask for questions with brackets.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-no\-brackets\fR
Ask for questions that group nothing in brackets. Of
.B \-b
and
.BR \-B ,
the one given last counts.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-max\fR \fIN\fR
Keep every number, and every step of working a question out, within
.IR N ,
from 10 to 10000.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-operators\fR \fILIST\fR
Use only these operators, given as a comma-separated list of
.BR add ,
.BR subtract ,
.BR multiply
and
.BR divide ,
each once.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-range\fR \fILOW\fR\-\fIHIGH\fR
Draw every answer from
.I LOW
to
.IR HIGH ,
both included. The numbers are whole numbers from 0 to 10000, at most 100
apart. With
.B \-m
an answer above that limit is refused.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-no\-negatives\fR
Ask for questions with no number below zero, in the question or on the way
to its answer.
.TP
\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-negatives\fR
Ask for questions that may have negative numbers. Of
.B \-n
and
.BR \-N ,
the one given last counts.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-feedback\fR
Say after each answer whether it was right, before the next question.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-working\fR
Show under each mistake in the result how it is worked out, from the task
down to the answer, one step after another. The API sends the working as JSON,
so a c=true in SAMATH_API_URL is left out when this is given. An older API
sends no working, and then nothing is shown.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-print\fR
Print the questions with their answers, one after another, instead of asking
them, for a worksheet or a key. The time limit, practice, feedback and working
do not apply to a printout.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAMATH_API_URL
Where the questions are fetched from. The default is
.BR http://localhost:3000/gen?c=true .
The value has to be an
.B http
or
.B https
address. It is handed to
.BR curl (1)
as it is.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The run was finished or stopped with
.BR Q ,
whatever the score, or for
.BR \-\-help " or " \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
The command line is wrong, the questions could not be fetched, there was
not enough memory to keep or practise the mistakes, standard input could not
be read, or the result could not be written out.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I contrib/samath.bash
Bash completion for the options and the operator names.
.B make install
puts it in
.IR $PREFIX/share/bash-completion/completions ,
where bash-completion finds it; otherwise source it from
.IR ~/.bashrc .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A POSIX system with
.BR curl (1)
7.21 or newer on
.BR PATH ,
and a running SaMathAPI. On Windows, run it under WSL.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1)
